  "word_count": 133,
  "text_content": "Ngozi kept a brown hen in a wooden coop beside her house. The hen had seven little chicks with soft yellow feathers. Every morning, the chicks followed their mother and pecked at the ground. One afternoon, a hawk circled high above the yard. The hen clucked loudly when she saw it. Her chicks heard the warning and ran to her at once. She spread her wings wide and covered them all. The hawk swooped down, but it could not reach the chicks. It flew away over the bush. Ngozi ran out of the house with a stick in her hand. She counted the chicks one by one, and every chick was safe. That evening, she shut the coop and gave the hen some extra corn. A good mother always protects her little ones.",
